== Notes ==
* {{dlc|r}} Upon pickup, Golden Pennies have a <math>0.98^{(n-1)}</math> chance to spawn another Golden Penny, where <math>n</math> represents the number of times it has been picked up.
** The minimum possible amount of cents from a Golden Penny is 2, while the maximum is theoretically infinite. On average, Golden Pennies give ~9 cents.
* {{dlc|anr+}} Unlocking [[#Sticky Nickel|Sticky Nickels]] is strictly speaking a downgrade, as they replace normal Nickels, though the sticky ones are rare enough to not make a severe difference.
* {{dlc|a}} If Lucky Pennies have not been unlocked, they will always be replaced by a Penny in any room layouts containing them.
** {{dlc|r}} Golden Pennies will also be replaced by random Coin pickup if not unlocked yet.
* {{dlc|a+}} [[Booster Pack#5]] added a green glow to Lucky Pennies, making them easier to spot. This was from [https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1173905740 this Steam Workshop mod] by piber20.
* {{E|Ultra Greed}} and [[Ultra Greed#Ultra Greedier|his statue]] cannot pick up Sticky Nickels until they have been unstuck by an explosion, thus negating some difficulty from the fight.
** During the Ultra Greed fight, if a Sticky Nickel drops, Ultra Greed will be continuously drawn to it.
** {{e|Bumbino}} also has this behaviour.
* {{dlc|r}} Sticky Nickels visibly stick to the ground upon spawning, making them easier to distinguish from ordinary Nickels.
* {{dlc+|r}} {{i|Sack Head}} can cause a Golden Penny to spawn a [[sack]] instead of another Golden Penny.{{dlc-}}
* The probabilities in the table refer to the kind of coin that is generated by the game when a coin is spawned with a sub-type of 0 (i.e. a random coin).

